{"number": 139, "text": "             20.3\n                      1 grow                        4 close friends\n                      2 to be/fall madly in love    5 keep in touch with\n                      3 accept a proposal\n                      The gaps can be filled in the following ways. The answers are, of course, private and personal!\n             20.4\n                      1 sight     4 life\n                      2  make     5 returned\n                      3 fell      6 have\n\n             20.5\n                      Possible collocations:\n                      love                                    friend\n                      to make love                            my  best friend\n                      to love someone deeply                  an old friend\n                      to send someone  your love              a childhood friend\n                                                               a true friend\n\n                      friendship                              relationship\n                      a lasting friendship                    a good relationship\n                      to hold out the hand of friendship      to end a relationship\n                      to value someone’s friendship           a family relationship\n\n\n                      Unit  21\n              21.1\n                      1  fully-furnished accommodation        4 astudio flat\n                      2  short-let accommodation              5 off-road parking\n                      3  aresidential area                    6 a fully-fitted kitchen\n              21.2\n                      1  We want to turn our garage into a granny flat.\n                      2  Harper has invited me to her house-warming party.\n                      3  Next week | have to move out of my flat.\n                      4  Xavier makes a business out of doing up old houses.\n                      5  Our bedroom  overlooks the garden.\n                      6  Our house needs to be completely refurbished.\n                      7        that one day I’ll have a place of my own.\n                      8  The bank can help if you want to take out a mortgage.\n              21,3\n                          We  live on a busy road, but we’re lucky because we have off-road parking.\n\n                          Gemma   has moved  out of her old flat and has now got a new place in Walville Street.\n                          We’re building an extension to our house which will give us a bigger kitchen.\n                          The flat is fully furnished, which is good because | have no furniture of my own.\n                          She had to take out a big mortgage as the house was very expensive.\n                          There is no affordable housing for young people in this area; prices are ridiculously high.\n                          New  people have moved  into the house next door. | haven’t met them yet.\n                          It’s a very spacious apartment with a huge living room and a big kitchen.\n                          The flat is available to rent from the first of March onwards.\n                        Xe)\n                          My  brother and his wife live in a draughty old cottage.\n                       10\n\n              21.4\n                      Your dream  home   could be waiting for you at Highdale Cottages. All cottages have a view of the\n                       River Marn. Ideal for anyone seeking a second home in the area.\n                      Telephone  3340251 for appointments to view.\n              21.5\n                         ... welcome her home.            4 ...make  yourself at home.\n                       1\n                         ... leave home / move out.       5... feel homesick.\n                       2\n                         ... feel at home.\n                       3\n\n\n                                                                       English Collocations in Use Inte